(3545763, 495351, 40053, '<td valign="top">I wish that the depth of field in this were such that at least the closest two boats were in sharp focus.  the closest boat being out of focus is very distracting.  The compesition and colors are very nice</td>', 'I wish that the depth of field in this were such that at least the closest two boats were in sharp focus.  the closest boat being out of focus is very distracting.  The compesition and colors are very nice', '2007-04-13 14:39:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545766, 496138, 5792, '<td valign="top">Ahhhh... Oregon State! You realize, of course, that all U of O grads will give this a 1, don''t you? LOL!!! Nicely captured and framed.<br/> <br/>Positives:<br/>Lighting and tonality are both very good. The buiding is a worthy photographic subject with a lot of interesting detail.<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>Composition is nice, particularly that you took care to frame the foregound walkways balanced in the image. Center framing is right for this picture.<br/> <br/>It is a bit confusing for the viewer as to whether this image is intended to be full color, muted color or sepia toned. The rest is fine.<br/> <br/>The Challenge:<br/>Meets the challenge withouty doubt. Being well toned and meeting the challenge is not enough. DPCers want some thing spectacular in the images they see. You have to include ''added value'' to set your composition apart from the rest for a higher score. DPCers are harsh voters.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>I would review the color/duotone nature of this image and make a concious decision to exaggerate it to be unmistakably one way or another. Make it plainly a sepia, B&amp;W or more vibrantly colored.<br/> <br/>I don''t know your settings but taking a longer exposed image at a large f-number like f/22 will create more exaggerated star patterns around the lights that are popular at DPC. Those can be ''enhanced'' in RAW and/or post processing for more effect.<br/> <br/>For added viewer interest you might consider including some students walking toward the the bulding on the sidewalks.. maybe a solidary student with a pack full of books on one walkway and a couple arm in arm on the other.<br/> <br/>You might consider experimenting with other perspectives on the building, including this same one except clipping off part of the wings to make a larger framing of the building center. That would allow a more traditional aspect ratio for the composition and include more detail from the building itself.</td>', 'Ahhhh... Oregon State! You realize, of course, that all U of O grads will give this a 1, don''t you? LOL!!! Nicely captured and framed. Positives:Lighting and tonality are both very good. The buiding is a worthy photographic subject with a lot of interesting detail. Technicals:Composition is nice, particularly that you took care to frame the foregound walkways balanced in the image. Center framing is right for this picture. It is a bit confusing for the viewer as to whether this image is intended to be full color, muted color or sepia toned. The rest is fine. The Challenge:Meets the challenge withouty doubt. Being well toned and meeting the challenge is not enough. DPCers want some thing spectacular in the images they see. You have to include ''added value'' to set your composition apart from the rest for a higher score. DPCers are harsh voters. Suggestions:I would review the color/duotone nature of this image and make a concious decision to exaggerate it to be unmistakably one way or another. Make it plainly a sepia, B&W or more vibrantly colored. I don''t know your settings but taking a longer exposed image at a large f-number like f/22 will create more exaggerated star patterns around the lights that are popular at DPC. Those can be ''enhanced'' in RAW and/or post processing for more effect. For added viewer interest you might consider including some students walking toward the the bulding on the sidewalks.. maybe a solidary student with a pack full of books on one walkway and a couple arm in arm on the other. You might consider experimenting with other perspectives on the building, including this same one except clipping off part of the wings to make a larger framing of the building center. That would allow a more traditional aspect ratio for the composition and include more detail from the building itself.', '2007-04-13 14:40:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545771, 495526, 40053, '<td valign="top">I really like the steam from the stacks, but find that the blue lights at the bottom are very distracting, maybe if it were cropped closer an higher so there are less of them, the impact would have been stronger.</td>', 'I really like the steam from the stacks, but find that the blue lights at the bottom are very distracting, maybe if it were cropped closer an higher so there are less of them, the impact would have been stronger.', '2007-04-13 14:48:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545772, 494923, 40053, '<td valign="top">This shots too easy.  I''ve seen it EVERYWHERE.  The exposure is nice though.</td>', 'This shots too easy.  I''ve seen it EVERYWHERE.  The exposure is nice though.', '2007-04-13 14:49:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545777, 496118, 40053, '<td valign="top">This shot feels like it stopped loading.  The cropping on the bottom is too tight...i guess i feel like it needs more interest?</td>', 'This shot feels like it stopped loading.  The cropping on the bottom is too tight...i guess i feel like it needs more interest?', '2007-04-13 14:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545786, 495998, 40053, '<td valign="top">This shot was so close, the lights are too hot though, so it distracts from everything else.  the colors on the memorial and the bridge are beautiful.</td>', 'This shot was so close, the lights are too hot though, so it distracts from everything else.  the colors on the memorial and the bridge are beautiful.', '2007-04-13 15:00:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545794, 495777, 40053, '<td valign="top">This image would have been much more impactful if you''d left the headlights off...would have shifted the focus entirely on the escape.</td>', 'This image would have been much more impactful if you''d left the headlights off...would have shifted the focus entirely on the escape.', '2007-04-13 15:04:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545795, 494923, 39679, '<td valign="top">Living in Seattle myself, I''ve seen this shot dozens of times but your''s is really well composed and you nailed the white balance. Well done.</td>', 'Living in Seattle myself, I''ve seen this shot dozens of times but your''s is really well composed and you nailed the white balance. Well done.', '2007-04-13 15:05:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545797, 494697, 39679, '<td valign="top">Great job accenting the blue.  It really furthers the feeling of a cold night.</td>', 'Great job accenting the blue.  It really furthers the feeling of a cold night.', '2007-04-13 15:06:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545798, 496133, 40053, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, and I like the compesition, but it seems ever so slightly out of focus.</td>', 'I like the idea, and I like the compesition, but it seems ever so slightly out of focus.', '2007-04-13 15:06:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545801, 494599, 39679, '<td valign="top">If this were in focus it''d be a really good shot.  Nice use of lighting.</td>', 'If this were in focus it''d be a really good shot.  Nice use of lighting.', '2007-04-13 15:08:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545813, 494128, 39679, '<td valign="top">This is a good concept.  I like the way you''ve (intentionally or not) used the reflection on the path as a leading line but the exposure is really dark and the light is so bright that it just overpowers everything else.  I''d love to see this again if you could use a gradiated filter to reduce the brightness of the light and allow the path to really stand out.</td>', 'This is a good concept.  I like the way you''ve (intentionally or not) used the reflection on the path as a leading line but the exposure is really dark and the light is so bright that it just overpowers everything else.  I''d love to see this again if you could use a gradiated filter to reduce the brightness of the light and allow the path to really stand out.', '2007-04-13 15:12:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545816, 493755, 40053, '<td valign="top">The color and exposure on this are very impressive.  My feeling is that it needs to be cropped even tighter, on the left and the bottom.</td>', 'The color and exposure on this are very impressive.  My feeling is that it needs to be cropped even tighter, on the left and the bottom.', '2007-04-13 15:14:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3545818, 494809, 72812, '<td valign="top">This is one of those photos that caused me to stop and think.  I mean that in a good way.  You did a good job of conveying an emotion.  Good lighting and framing.  It makes me wonder what she is running from... where she is running to.  The color tone works great for this pic too.  The cases in the lower right do start to wash out a bit, but it does not take away from the overall photo in my opinion.  Really nice job.  So is she taking "the midnight train goin anywhere..."? Nice work on this one.</td>', 'This is one of those photos that caused me to stop and think.  I mean that in a good way.  You did a good job of conveying an emotion.  Good lighting and framing.  It makes me wonder what she is running from... where she is running to.  The color tone works great for this pic too.  The cases in the lower right do start to wash out a bit, but it does not take away from the overall photo in my opinion.  Really nice job.  So is she taking "the midnight train goin anywhere..."? Nice work on this one.', '2007-04-13 15:15:50.000000', NULL, 1),
