(3548342, 493608, 53316, '<td valign="top"><b>Fantastic!!!!</b> Definitely a 10 from me.  Just today I read in The Walrus (magazine) about Roger Ballen, and this reminds me of the photos of his in the article.<br/>Here are the links but I think you have to be a subscriber to access the stuff.  (<a href="//www.walrusmagazine.com/u/register/teaser.php?ref=detail-wild-chamber" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">1</a> and <a href="//www.walrusmagazine.com/articles/online-exclusive-detail-gallery-tk/1/4/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">2</a>)  <a href="//www.rogerballen.com/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Here</a> is Ballen''s own website though.  New Project and Shadow Chamber, in the image gallery section, are closest in style to what I saw in the article although I don''t see any from the article there.<br/>So yes. What I am saying is that this image reminds me of a famous photographer''s images, which is super awesome!!  I would add it to my favorites but I am currently at my max limit.</td>', 'Fantastic!!!! Definitely a 10 from me.  Just today I read in The Walrus (magazine) about Roger Ballen, and this reminds me of the photos of his in the article.Here are the links but I think you have to be a subscriber to access the stuff.  (1 and 2)  Here is Ballen''s own website though.  New Project and Shadow Chamber, in the image gallery section, are closest in style to what I saw in the article although I don''t see any from the article there.So yes. What I am saying is that this image reminds me of a famous photographer''s images, which is super awesome!!  I would add it to my favorites but I am currently at my max limit.', '2007-04-14 23:13:12.000000', NULL, 1),
