(3563757, 495642, 5792, '<td valign="top"><b>Positives:</b> <br/>Wonderfully conceived and captured black and white. Subtlely moody and gives the viewer much to think about when looking at it. It is the type of image that draws the viewer back again and again. Technical quality is excellent. The immensity of the cobblestones in the frame stuns the viewer.<br/> <br/><b>Technicals:</b> <br/>Black and white contrast and range is just right. Your processing enhances the moodiness of the composition. Backlighting and shadows enhance the composition greatly.<br/> <br/>The depth of field on this one is interesting. One of the few images where major subjects like the two people remaining out of focus fits the composition. Generally speaking you''d normally have the closest foreground in sharpest focus but that is not the case here. It is slightly out of focus. Don''t know if that is by design. It certainly doesn''t hurt the composition and adds a more curiosity to the picture.  <br/> <br/><b>The Challenge:</b> <br/>Certainly meets the challenge well and in a unique and interesting way. Commenters obviously like this image a lot and say so. The average score is low, but that is true of most DPC images. Perhaps voters glossed over this one because it lacks the flash and instant "Wow factor" DPC voters have come to expect.<br/> <br/>I voted this challenge and gave this image a 9 and probably should have given it a 10. Its one fine image.<br/> <br/><b>Suggestions:</b> <br/>The reason I know I should have scored this a 10 is because I can''t think of anything significant to suggest to improve it.</td>', 'Positives: Wonderfully conceived and captured black and white. Subtlely moody and gives the viewer much to think about when looking at it. It is the type of image that draws the viewer back again and again. Technical quality is excellent. The immensity of the cobblestones in the frame stuns the viewer. Technicals: Black and white contrast and range is just right. Your processing enhances the moodiness of the composition. Backlighting and shadows enhance the composition greatly. The depth of field on this one is interesting. One of the few images where major subjects like the two people remaining out of focus fits the composition. Generally speaking you''d normally have the closest foreground in sharpest focus but that is not the case here. It is slightly out of focus. Don''t know if that is by design. It certainly doesn''t hurt the composition and adds a more curiosity to the picture.   The Challenge: Certainly meets the challenge well and in a unique and interesting way. Commenters obviously like this image a lot and say so. The average score is low, but that is true of most DPC images. Perhaps voters glossed over this one because it lacks the flash and instant "Wow factor" DPC voters have come to expect. I voted this challenge and gave this image a 9 and probably should have given it a 10. Its one fine image. Suggestions: The reason I know I should have scored this a 10 is because I can''t think of anything significant to suggest to improve it.', '2007-04-19 17:38:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3563829, 494276, 41337, '<td valign="top">Wazztastic!</td>', 'Wazztastic!', '2007-04-19 18:09:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3563842, 495877, 54778, '<td valign="top">Excellent interpretation of the challenge.. the slight destat works well here.. very moving pic...</td>', 'Excellent interpretation of the challenge.. the slight destat works well here.. very moving pic...', '2007-04-19 18:16:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3563866, 495642, 61651, '<td valign="top">Saw this in stdavidson''s critique thread and was reminded that I had never got to comment on it, so I''ll rectify that here.  I voted this a 9, and really liked, as a number of commenters have already noted, the moodiness and mystery of the shot.  Not making the people the focus of the image is key to its success for me, as is the lighting.  Including the people, however marginally, did have the added benefit of provoking me to "hear" the image - that sounds crazy, but with the strong focus on the cobblestones and background hint at the pedestrians, the image moved me to recall the sound of footsteps on cobblestones.  It''s not every day an image comes with its own soundtrack!<br/> <br/>My only quibble, and keep in mind it is minor - is that one of your pedestrians is carrying a pocketbook that I happen to find somewhat distracting in the image.<br/> <br/>I just read some of your comments again and notice someone else noted "hearing" the cobblestones, too. :)</td>', 'Saw this in stdavidson''s critique thread and was reminded that I had never got to comment on it, so I''ll rectify that here.  I voted this a 9, and really liked, as a number of commenters have already noted, the moodiness and mystery of the shot.  Not making the people the focus of the image is key to its success for me, as is the lighting.  Including the people, however marginally, did have the added benefit of provoking me to "hear" the image - that sounds crazy, but with the strong focus on the cobblestones and background hint at the pedestrians, the image moved me to recall the sound of footsteps on cobblestones.  It''s not every day an image comes with its own soundtrack! My only quibble, and keep in mind it is minor - is that one of your pedestrians is carrying a pocketbook that I happen to find somewhat distracting in the image. I just read some of your comments again and notice someone else noted "hearing" the cobblestones, too. :)', '2007-04-19 18:28:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3563918, 495497, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great work! Amazing shot. You have a great notion of visualizing the shot. Truly unique and glad it did so well for you<br/> <br/>I am guessing the low scores were because it was "Basic" and many didn''t deem it basic. Too bad it wasn''t advanced, because some people just don''t give the benefit of the doubt.</td>', 'Great work! Amazing shot. You have a great notion of visualizing the shot. Truly unique and glad it did so well for you I am guessing the low scores were because it was "Basic" and many didn''t deem it basic. Too bad it wasn''t advanced, because some people just don''t give the benefit of the doubt.', '2007-04-19 18:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3563924, 496090, 62318, '<td valign="top">Technically a well done shot. Not sure I like the borders myself, but that is such a minor thing. Good lighting and a nice fit to the challenge.</td>', 'Technically a well done shot. Not sure I like the borders myself, but that is such a minor thing. Good lighting and a nice fit to the challenge.', '2007-04-19 18:49:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3563950, 496035, 62318, '<td valign="top">I think purple is the new black (I''ve been using it a lot my self). :) Very nice atmospheric mood in this one. Love the repeating shapes, but what really wins this for me is that one shutter is closed the other open. Wonderful shot and under-rated in my opinion.</td>', 'I think purple is the new black (I''ve been using it a lot my self). :) Very nice atmospheric mood in this one. Love the repeating shapes, but what really wins this for me is that one shutter is closed the other open. Wonderful shot and under-rated in my opinion.', '2007-04-19 18:58:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564121, 496073, 60495, '<td valign="top">I really like this one, the similarities and differences between the two floors are fascinating. congrats!</td>', 'I really like this one, the similarities and differences between the two floors are fascinating. congrats!', '2007-04-19 20:24:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564155, 496073, 27763, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot.  Sorry to see it didn''t ribbon.</td>', 'I like this a lot.  Sorry to see it didn''t ribbon.', '2007-04-19 20:37:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564521, 495091, 68119, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all of your comments.  This is a PB which i am wrapped about.</td>', 'Thanks for all of your comments.  This is a PB which i am wrapped about.', '2007-04-19 23:01:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564534, 494261, 51938, '<td valign="top">Congrats !! couldn''t have done more justice to the monument :-)</td>', 'Congrats !! couldn''t have done more justice to the monument :-)', '2007-04-19 23:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564555, 494261, 77091, '<td valign="top">This so beautiful in a very Art Deco-Batmanesque way.</td>', 'This so beautiful in a very Art Deco-Batmanesque way.', '2007-04-19 23:11:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564730, 496090, 64994, '<td valign="top">Jeb, another very cool shot, I really love the gradual darkening from left to right...if I had taken this the highlights would be blown and the shadows would be without feature, lol. Seriously, very nice and the DOF is very good!! Also, I really like the fact that the arch in the foreground bridge almost perfectly frames two archs in the background bridge, very nice composition. Way to go!!</td>', 'Jeb, another very cool shot, I really love the gradual darkening from left to right...if I had taken this the highlights would be blown and the shadows would be without feature, lol. Seriously, very nice and the DOF is very good!! Also, I really like the fact that the arch in the foreground bridge almost perfectly frames two archs in the background bridge, very nice composition. Way to go!!', '2007-04-20 00:24:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564731, 496090, 60862, '<td valign="top">Well, I voted this a 6 - looks like the masses were there and above. Congrats on a nice image. :)<br/> <br/>I wonder how it would look with the sky totally cropped out, so the arch of the first bridge frames the others?</td>', 'Well, I voted this a 6 - looks like the masses were there and above. Congrats on a nice image. :) I wonder how it would look with the sky totally cropped out, so the arch of the first bridge frames the others?', '2007-04-20 00:24:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3564780, 494261, 48138, '<td valign="top">Hey, I saw your statue on 30 Rock today.  This is a great photo.</td>', 'Hey, I saw your statue on 30 Rock today.  This is a great photo.', '2007-04-20 00:44:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3565192, 494261, 75510, '<td valign="top">excellent!</td>', 'excellent!', '2007-04-20 05:56:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3565196, 495642, 66635, '<td valign="top">Really nice.  Love the lighting and the mood.</td>', 'Really nice.  Love the lighting and the mood.', '2007-04-20 06:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3565532, 494276, 71550, '<td valign="top">Beautiful</td>', 'Beautiful', '2007-04-20 09:59:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3565533, 495618, 30982, '<td valign="top">Yay!  This most certainly did not bomb.  Glad to see something outside of the glitzy city lights reflected in the river (good shots just the same) do well!  I quite like the color and busy-ness of it.</td>', 'Yay!  This most certainly did not bomb.  Glad to see something outside of the glitzy city lights reflected in the river (good shots just the same) do well!  I quite like the color and busy-ness of it.', '2007-04-20 09:59:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3565688, 496073, 26001, '<td valign="top">Good to see this one do well. this was one of my favourites. congrats!</td>', 'Good to see this one do well. this was one of my favourites. congrats!', '2007-04-20 11:05:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3566024, 494923, 77244, '<td valign="top">Great clarity, nice location to shoot.. good work</td>', 'Great clarity, nice location to shoot.. good work', '2007-04-20 13:18:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3566725, 494330, 67145, '<td valign="top">wow adam ... absolutely beautiful photograph ... stunning ... and congrats on a 39th place ... pretty good considering the competition ...</td>', 'wow adam ... absolutely beautiful photograph ... stunning ... and congrats on a 39th place ... pretty good considering the competition ...', '2007-04-20 17:55:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3567359, 495570, 35334, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a wonderful image. I get a great sense of action at night. I''m not sure what is going on here--but that is characteristic of the experience of night. <br/> <br/>I gave the image a 10. I really love it. But I seem to be the only person who gave it a 10. I can understand why this image did not do well in a DPC challenge called "Night Shot"--it certainly is not a typical night image. But among those who tried to push the boundaries, I thought this was the best.<br/> <br/>DanW</td>', 'I thought this was a wonderful image. I get a great sense of action at night. I''m not sure what is going on here--but that is characteristic of the experience of night.  I gave the image a 10. I really love it. But I seem to be the only person who gave it a 10. I can understand why this image did not do well in a DPC challenge called "Night Shot"--it certainly is not a typical night image. But among those who tried to push the boundaries, I thought this was the best. DanW', '2007-04-20 23:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3567664, 494276, 63244, '<td valign="top">E - I loved this the moment I saw it.  GORGEOUS! The colors are brilliant, DOF and aspect make this so appealing. (Guess you didn''t find the mine, huh. ROFL!)</td>', 'E - I loved this the moment I saw it.  GORGEOUS! The colors are brilliant, DOF and aspect make this so appealing. (Guess you didn''t find the mine, huh. ROFL!)', '2007-04-21 01:25:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3567740, 496073, 66635, '<td valign="top">Really neat.  Love the color and the mood.</td>', 'Really neat.  Love the color and the mood.', '2007-04-21 01:57:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3568705, 494276, 554, '<td valign="top">Am I the only one that thinks it looks tilted?</td>', 'Am I the only one that thinks it looks tilted?', '2007-04-21 14:07:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3568736, 494276, 50231, '<td valign="top">David the cactus is tilted as it was the way it grew on the uneven terrain. The horizon however is level.</td>', 'David the cactus is tilted as it was the way it grew on the uneven terrain. The horizon however is level.', '2007-04-21 14:13:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3568763, 494276, 554, '<td valign="top">Yes. I thought that.  I''m in no way ridiculing the nice photo.  It just looks tilted even with the cactus removed.</td>', 'Yes. I thought that.  I''m in no way ridiculing the nice photo.  It just looks tilted even with the cactus removed.', '2007-04-21 14:19:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3570115, 494599, 18450, '<td valign="top">Imaginative and creative approach to the challenge! Lighting and colours are awesome. Focus on the egg is a bit too blurry this time ...... looking forward to seeing more from you.</td>', 'Imaginative and creative approach to the challenge! Lighting and colours are awesome. Focus on the egg is a bit too blurry this time ...... looking forward to seeing more from you.', '2007-04-22 07:44:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3570166, 494809, 8367, '<td valign="top">A wonderful emotive capture. Great job!<br/>Love your sepia tones.<br/></td>', 'A wonderful emotive capture. Great job!Love your sepia tones.', '2007-04-22 09:12:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3570393, 494938, 35322, '<td valign="top">wow, this is great! When I first saw the pic (first 2 secs), I thought it was an iluminated palm tree, but then I realized they are fireworks! I just love what you have captured here. Excellent!</td>', 'wow, this is great! When I first saw the pic (first 2 secs), I thought it was an iluminated palm tree, but then I realized they are fireworks! I just love what you have captured here. Excellent!', '2007-04-22 12:19:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3570683, 494276, 8125, '<td valign="top">Congrats Erick!  Way to go with a well deserved blue!  This sure is beautiful; my one wish before leaving AZ is getting a night shot of the Supes.  I''ll just enjoy looking at yours.  :-)</td>', 'Congrats Erick!  Way to go with a well deserved blue!  This sure is beautiful; my one wish before leaving AZ is getting a night shot of the Supes.  I''ll just enjoy looking at yours.  :-)', '2007-04-22 14:51:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3570709, 495874, 21124, '<td valign="top">Original picture:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=501120" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/501120.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/501120.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/21124/thumb/501120.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Original picture:', '2007-04-22 15:20:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3571227, 493685, 70828, '<td valign="top">I, personally, think that the soft focus and the darkness works perfectly for this image. It makes me feel like a person seeing this IRL and about to exit the room QUIETLY so he can crash. I think the blend of tones from bottom to top and the softness of the blend is SUPER. I disagree with every negative comment that was made during the challenge. I would be proud to have created this very real image ...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-22 19:38:00.</i></td>', 'I, personally, think that the soft focus and the darkness works perfectly for this image. It makes me feel like a person seeing this IRL and about to exit the room QUIETLY so he can crash. I think the blend of tones from bottom to top and the softness of the blend is SUPER. I disagree with every negative comment that was made during the challenge. I would be proud to have created this very real image ...', '2007-04-22 20:31:49.000000', '2007-04-22 20:38:00.000000', 0),
(3571358, 495618, 44877, '<td valign="top">You''re right that this is not very dpc-esque, however I think it''s excellent and am glad it didn''t bomb as you expected... though I feel it would have deserved a better score for the creativity and the artistic feel of the photo. Awesome work.</td>', 'You''re right that this is not very dpc-esque, however I think it''s excellent and am glad it didn''t bomb as you expected... though I feel it would have deserved a better score for the creativity and the artistic feel of the photo. Awesome work.', '2007-04-22 21:38:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3571361, 495597, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GoddessBePhotos:</b></div><hr/><i> One word....this picture should have stayed in Vegas.... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>ummmmmm that is....more than one word....</td>', 'Originally posted by GoddessBePhotos: One word....this picture should have stayed in Vegas....   ummmmmm that is....more than one word....', '2007-04-22 21:40:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3571419, 495597, 93, '<td valign="top">I''m ecstatic to see that there are still *some* people out there that value humor over placing :)<br/> <br/>I laugh.</td>', 'I''m ecstatic to see that there are still *some* people out there that value humor over placing :) I laugh.', '2007-04-22 21:55:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3572225, 495363, 72142, '<td valign="top">sweet shot.</td>', 'sweet shot.', '2007-04-23 02:00:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3572243, 495641, 31244, '<td valign="top">One of the best pictures in this challenge. Thank you for not falling into the loop and becoming a score-whore. Respect.</td>', 'One of the best pictures in this challenge. Thank you for not falling into the loop and becoming a score-whore. Respect.', '2007-04-23 02:10:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3572629, 494276, 57060, '<td valign="top">Congrats ona fantastic shot and your ribbon!<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'Congrats ona fantastic shot and your ribbon! Jack', '2007-04-23 07:27:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3573010, 495363, 67043, '<td valign="top">Congrats! This is now my desktop wallpaper and I have gotten several comment from co-workers.<br/> <br/>X</td>', 'Congrats! This is now my desktop wallpaper and I have gotten several comment from co-workers. X', '2007-04-23 10:24:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3577370, 492918, 50695, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>This is a beautiful photo, truly beautiful. I just love the seemingly endless play of diagonals, thing and shadow, darkness and light, the confusion of perspective, the impossible height. You''ve created a stairway to heaven here.<br/> <br/>So as they''ve said, make the picture bigger next time! resize the largest dimension to 640 pixels (sometimes 720, depending on the challenge).<br/> <br/>Just based on this photo, I sincerely hope you come back for more challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from Critique Club  This is a beautiful photo, truly beautiful. I just love the seemingly endless play of diagonals, thing and shadow, darkness and light, the confusion of perspective, the impossible height. You''ve created a stairway to heaven here. So as they''ve said, make the picture bigger next time! resize the largest dimension to 640 pixels (sometimes 720, depending on the challenge). Just based on this photo, I sincerely hope you come back for more challenges.', '2007-04-24 15:29:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3577854, 494938, 58473, '<td valign="top">Beauty capture. I too saw a palm tree at first glance. Outstanding work.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Beauty capture. I too saw a palm tree at first glance. Outstanding work. ', '2007-04-24 17:53:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3578011, 494741, 55956, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from critique club</b> <br/> <br/>Hi, sorry for your result in the challenge but is really difficult see something in this image.     <br/>The image is too much dark and there are too few details. This the only critique that i can write. I think that you wish show a bridge on the sea (is this the truth?) not a bad idea. <br/>If the photograph information are true I think that you can obtain better result with a tripode and a higher exposure time. <br/>Iso 1600 are too much high and you will have too noise in the image.<br/> <br/>Best Regards<br/>Gennaro<br/> <br/>P.S. for any question send me a private message</td>', 'Greetings from critique club  Hi, sorry for your result in the challenge but is really difficult see something in this image.     The image is too much dark and there are too few details. This the only critique that i can write. I think that you wish show a bridge on the sea (is this the truth?) not a bad idea. If the photograph information are true I think that you can obtain better result with a tripode and a higher exposure time. Iso 1600 are too much high and you will have too noise in the image. Best RegardsGennaro P.S. for any question send me a private message', '2007-04-24 18:42:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3581396, 494809, 17148, '<td valign="top">Love the lighting...great shot and story here</td>', 'Love the lighting...great shot and story here', '2007-04-25 12:35:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3582553, 495497, 62095, '<td valign="top">A great symettrical piece here.  Good use of the reflections, and very clever setup!<br/> <br/></td>', 'A great symettrical piece here.  Good use of the reflections, and very clever setup! ', '2007-04-25 17:25:32.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3583981, 494180, 62318, '<td valign="top">Wonderful juxtaposition. A skyline with a sense of humor. Surprised you didn''t get more comments though, because it is a terrific photo.</td>', 'Wonderful juxtaposition. A skyline with a sense of humor. Surprised you didn''t get more comments though, because it is a terrific photo.', '2007-04-26 01:54:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3585854, 493685, 5792, '<td valign="top">You got a 4. Since scoring in this challenge was about the DPC norm that indicates the group thought your image "sucks". Since an Arizonan got the blue in that challenge then voters obviously got things right.<br/> <br/>It is likely they thought it was a chintsy, last second setup and oversmoothed by noise reduction. I liked the composition and felt the noise reduction, though overdone, supported the image concept. I gave it a 7 which in my world means it is average. It met the challege and does not have any super serious technical defects. Reviewing it again doesn''t give me any reason to change my mind. :)</td>', 'You got a 4. Since scoring in this challenge was about the DPC norm that indicates the group thought your image "sucks". Since an Arizonan got the blue in that challenge then voters obviously got things right. It is likely they thought it was a chintsy, last second setup and oversmoothed by noise reduction. I liked the composition and felt the noise reduction, though overdone, supported the image concept. I gave it a 7 which in my world means it is average. It met the challege and does not have any super serious technical defects. Reviewing it again doesn''t give me any reason to change my mind. :)', '2007-04-26 17:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3589193, 493754, 72317, '<td valign="top">If you had used a lower ISO and a setting better suited to shooting in the dark, I''m sure this would''ve scored very high. A tripod would''ve also helped, or even the hood of a car.. A trash can. Just something to set the camera on. Self timer completely diminishes hand shake with a tripod or an elevated surface. I really like the color of the sky, though. And the way it blends. This is not bad at all for a first challenge. Better than me, anyways.</td>', 'If you had used a lower ISO and a setting better suited to shooting in the dark, I''m sure this would''ve scored very high. A tripod would''ve also helped, or even the hood of a car.. A trash can. Just something to set the camera on. Self timer completely diminishes hand shake with a tripod or an elevated surface. I really like the color of the sky, though. And the way it blends. This is not bad at all for a first challenge. Better than me, anyways.', '2007-04-27 21:08:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3591979, 495606, 48560, '<td valign="top">you''re right, that rock DOES have that "i was added in during post-processing" look! very out of place, very odd.<br/> <br/>p/s: why are you always out under bridges at night? :p</td>', 'you''re right, that rock DOES have that "i was added in during post-processing" look! very out of place, very odd. p/s: why are you always out under bridges at night? :p', '2007-04-29 09:55:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3596561, 495497, 67697, '<td valign="top">You know, when I voted on this during the challenge, I really liked it for the clarity and the reflections.  And I saw it was "validated" and I had no idea what on earth was wrong with it.  Well - gee - I sure am unobservant.  Knock on head - there is only ONE Washington Monument.  So - wow what a great pic! It''s very beautiful. Very clever way to design the pic.  Thanks for explaning how you did this.</td>', 'You know, when I voted on this during the challenge, I really liked it for the clarity and the reflections.  And I saw it was "validated" and I had no idea what on earth was wrong with it.  Well - gee - I sure am unobservant.  Knock on head - there is only ONE Washington Monument.  So - wow what a great pic! It''s very beautiful. Very clever way to design the pic.  Thanks for explaning how you did this.', '2007-04-30 16:41:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3602720, 492918, 28801, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I think the choice of monochrome is a good one as it helps to draw attention to the shapes that make up the image. In addition to what has been said before, probably more light would have helped to ''open'' up the image some more.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club I think the choice of monochrome is a good one as it helps to draw attention to the shapes that make up the image. In addition to what has been said before, probably more light would have helped to ''open'' up the image some more.', '2007-05-01 22:04:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3604608, 495641, 35669, '<td valign="top">looks like a cross section of the earth.<br/>this is just great, i really like what you do.</td>', 'looks like a cross section of the earth.this is just great, i really like what you do.', '2007-05-02 08:15:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3606323, 494599, 18080, '<td valign="top">in another challenge with a slightly better crisp focus (which you might have got with a little editing :), then this could be a top 20 shot.<br/>I love the idea of it, but the focus is like all of mine, soft.<br/>Keep going, you have the makings of a great photographer.<br/> <br/>Kev</td>', 'in another challenge with a slightly better crisp focus (which you might have got with a little editing :), then this could be a top 20 shot.I love the idea of it, but the focus is like all of mine, soft.Keep going, you have the makings of a great photographer. Kev', '2007-05-02 15:40:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3606449, 495382, 60732, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments kenskid and cheekymunky.  I submitted the photo here even though I knew it wouldn''t get a good rating - I had taken the photo even before I knew about the challenge anyway.  I thought it was an interesting photo and wanted to see if others thought so as well :-).</td>', 'Thanks for your comments kenskid and cheekymunky.  I submitted the photo here even though I knew it wouldn''t get a good rating - I had taken the photo even before I knew about the challenge anyway.  I thought it was an interesting photo and wanted to see if others thought so as well :-).', '2007-05-02 16:23:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3607649, 493794, 6519, '<td valign="top">Nathaniel, you had some very useful feedback in those comments. <br/> <br/>It is very much your own loss that you only choose to get upset, instead of stopping to think about how those comments might help you improve.</td>', 'Nathaniel, you had some very useful feedback in those comments.  It is very much your own loss that you only choose to get upset, instead of stopping to think about how those comments might help you improve.', '2007-05-02 20:36:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611234, 493794, 62925, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Fairfield20:</b></div><hr/><i> I cannot believe some people''s comments.<br/> <br/>Of course I used flash to take this picture! If I didn''t<br/> <br/>use flash the photo would be pitch black. It is very<br/> <br/>obvious by looking at the picture above that it was<br/> <br/>taken late at night. So what other light source can<br/> <br/>I use?  Seriously folks, let''s think before we leave<br/> <br/>comments.  And for those that didn''t find this interesting.<br/> <br/>That''s a matter of opinion. Very subjective. I''m sure<br/> <br/>If I looked at your portfolio, it''s very likely  <br/> <br/>that I would find boring photos there as well. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>maybe you should have thought before making that comment. You can use so many things as light sources, get creative</td>', 'Originally posted by Fairfield20: I cannot believe some people''s comments. Of course I used flash to take this picture! If I didn''t use flash the photo would be pitch black. It is very obvious by looking at the picture above that it was taken late at night. So what other light source can I use?  Seriously folks, let''s think before we leave comments.  And for those that didn''t find this interesting. That''s a matter of opinion. Very subjective. I''m sure If I looked at your portfolio, it''s very likely   that I would find boring photos there as well.  maybe you should have thought before making that comment. You can use so many things as light sources, get creative', '2007-05-03 16:41:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612781, 495212, 24111, '<td valign="top">This is great, love the story going on and the retro feel!</td>', 'This is great, love the story going on and the retro feel!', '2007-05-03 23:21:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3622172, 496052, 23458, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by timmi:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t get it. All the people who left negative comments about how tired they are of Nothern Lights shots... What is wrong with these people?  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>They are, quite simply, jealous. Jealous that they don''t live in the land of endless skies, stunning auroras, mountainscapes and outrageously good-looking blonde/blue eyed women. <br/> <br/>Quite frankly, I''m jealous too. 1 from me. :).<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by timmi: I don''t get it. All the people who left negative comments about how tired they are of Nothern Lights shots... What is wrong with these people?    They are, quite simply, jealous. Jealous that they don''t live in the land of endless skies, stunning auroras, mountainscapes and outrageously good-looking blonde/blue eyed women.  Quite frankly, I''m jealous too. 1 from me. :). ', '2007-05-06 23:12:04.000000', NULL, 0),
