(3684058, 496090, 48228, '<td valign="top">This one pleases me so much, and I love the moodyiness (if there is such a word) of this one..... <br/>I love also the dark mysterious colors that some of your image have, but here it works so well.<br/>I can also see another image here, by cropping off the dark sky completely, and making itlook more like a panarama. Give it a go and let me know as I love to see it.....</td>', 'This one pleases me so much, and I love the moodyiness (if there is such a word) of this one..... I love also the dark mysterious colors that some of your image have, but here it works so well.I can also see another image here, by cropping off the dark sky completely, and making itlook more like a panarama. Give it a go and let me know as I love to see it.....', '2007-05-23 03:40:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3695379, 494741, 78766, '<td valign="top">too dark but i tried something with this shot in PS and it came out neat. try adjust curves first, targetting the pole on the left. then turn the picture b/w. finally adjust brightness/contrast to raise up brightness and contrast till just right. then burn the background and edges black and dodge the poles white and try take a look!! the shot looks really, really kewl. i dont know if its against rule to do this so .....</td>', 'too dark but i tried something with this shot in PS and it came out neat. try adjust curves first, targetting the pole on the left. then turn the picture b/w. finally adjust brightness/contrast to raise up brightness and contrast till just right. then burn the background and edges black and dodge the poles white and try take a look!! the shot looks really, really kewl. i dont know if its against rule to do this so .....', '2007-05-25 17:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
