(4347327, 494276, 85886, '<td valign="top">I know this is a night shot, but how did you manage to shoot a 5.5 minute exposure wide open at 400 ISO and not overexpose?  Did you use a neutral density on your lens or was this just the ideal exposure time for the lighting levels at the scene?  Thanks!  N</td>', 'I know this is a night shot, but how did you manage to shoot a 5.5 minute exposure wide open at 400 ISO and not overexpose?  Did you use a neutral density on your lens or was this just the ideal exposure time for the lighting levels at the scene?  Thanks!  N', '2007-12-31 09:37:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4347840, 494276, 50231, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fastforward:</b></div><hr/><i>  Did you use a neutral density on your lens or was this just the ideal exposure time for the lighting levels at the scene?  Thanks!  N </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It was just ideal. It was about 9pm when the shot was taken. There was very little light except for the stars. I was shooting in bulb mode and just sort of flying by the seat of my pants. After the exposure recorded I checked the LCD and new I had a winner. I say it is better to be lucky than good. :-)<br/> <br/>Thanks for the question!</td>', 'Originally posted by fastforward:  Did you use a neutral density on your lens or was this just the ideal exposure time for the lighting levels at the scene?  Thanks!  N   It was just ideal. It was about 9pm when the shot was taken. There was very little light except for the stars. I was shooting in bulb mode and just sort of flying by the seat of my pants. After the exposure recorded I checked the LCD and new I had a winner. I say it is better to be lucky than good. :-) Thanks for the question!', '2007-12-31 14:05:56.000000', NULL, 0),
